==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
[[IPA]]: /'bera/

===Etymology===
From the West Germanic root ''*beran-'', from the Proto-Indo-European root ''*bher-'' (''brown animal''). Cognate with the Old High German ''[[bero]]'' (and New High German ''[[Bär]]''), the Middle Dutch ''bere'' (and Dutch ''[[beer]]''), and the Old Norse ''ber''. <!-- A North Germanic variant, ''*bernu-'', gave Old Norse {{Latinx|[[bjǫrn]]}} (cf. Swedish ''[[björn]]'').  The Proto-Indo-European root is also the source of the Common Slavic *''[[brlog]]'' (and thence, Russian [[берлога]], ''den''). -->

===Noun===
'''bera''' ''m'' (pl. ''beran'')

# [[bear]]

[[Category:Old English nouns]]

----

